      lessons: lessons('art-music-and-creativity', [
        "Module 1: Making art",
        ["Shapes, lines and colour", "text", 540, "## The art toolbox\nEvery picture is built from **lines, shapes and colours**.\n\n| Line | Feeling |\n|---|---|\n| Straight | Calm, strong |\n| Wavy | Gentle, flowing |\n| Zigzag | Exciting, sharp |\n| Thick | Bold |\n\n## The colour wheel\n{{cycle Red > Orange > Yellow > Green > Blue > Purple}}\n\n- **Primary colours:** red, yellow, blue.\n- **Secondary colours:** orange (red + yellow), green (yellow + blue), purple (red + blue).\n- **Warm colours:** red, orange, yellow. **Cool colours:** green, blue, purple.\n\n> Example: A sunny beach picture uses warm yellow and orange for the sand and cool blue for the sea.\n\n> Try it: What do you make if you mix blue and yellow? || Green.\n> Try it: Name two warm colours. || Any two of red, orange, yellow.", {"title": "Check your understanding", "questions": [{"prompt": "Which are the primary colours?", "options": ["Red, yellow, blue", "Green, orange, purple", "Black, white, grey", "Pink, brown, green"], "answer": 0, "why": "The three primaries."}, {"prompt": "Yellow + blue = ?", "options": ["Green", "Purple", "Orange", "Brown"], "answer": 0, "why": "Green."}, {"prompt": "Which colour is cool?", "options": ["Red", "Blue", "Orange", "Yellow"], "answer": 1, "why": "Blue is a cool colour."}]}],
        ["Drawing a scene", "text", 600, "## Make a picture with depth\nGreat scenes have a **foreground**, **middle ground** and **background**.\n\n{{stack Background: sky, hills, far trees | Middle ground: houses, river | Foreground: big flowers, a goat}}\n\n## Steps\n1. Draw the horizon line.\n2. Sketch big shapes first.\n3. Add details in the foreground.\n4. Colour from light to dark.\n\n> Tip: Things that are **far away** look smaller and lighter. Things that are **near** look bigger and clearer.\n\n> Example: A tall baobab tree in the foreground can look as large as a faraway mountain.\n\n> Try it: Draw a scene of your school using the foreground, middle ground and background. || Answers vary. Check that near things are bigger and far things are smaller.", {"title": "Check your understanding", "questions": [{"prompt": "Things that are far away look...", "options": ["Bigger", "Smaller", "The same", "Darker"], "answer": 1, "why": "Distance makes objects look smaller."}, {"prompt": "The foreground is...", "options": ["The part closest to you", "The sky", "The horizon", "The part far away"], "answer": 0, "why": "The nearest part."}, {"prompt": "Which comes first when drawing a scene?", "options": ["The horizon line", "Small details", "The signature", "The shading"], "answer": 0, "why": "Start with the horizon."}]}],
        "Module 2: Rhythm, stories and sharing",
        ["Finding your rhythm", "text", 540, "## Music is organised sound\n**Rhythm** is the pattern of long and short sounds. The **beat** is the steady pulse, like a heartbeat.\n\n| Note | Beats | Count |\n|---|---|---|\n| Whole note | 4 | 1-2-3-4 |\n| Half note | 2 | 1-2 |\n| Quarter note | 1 | 1 |\n\n{{chart Quarter:1 Half:2 Whole:4}}\n\n## Clap this pattern\n**Clap clap rest clap** (1 2 3 4). Repeat it four times.\n\n> Real life: Drummers across Tanzania use steady beats with changing patterns to tell stories and bring people together.\n\n> Try it: Clap a steady beat and say your name. How many claps does it take? || It depends on the syllables. \"A-mi-na\" has three claps.\n> Try it: How many quarter notes equal one whole note? || 4", {"title": "Check your understanding", "questions": [{"prompt": "The steady pulse in music is the...", "options": ["Melody", "Beat", "Lyric", "Silence"], "answer": 1, "why": "The beat."}, {"prompt": "A whole note lasts...", "options": ["1 beat", "2 beats", "4 beats", "8 beats"], "answer": 2, "why": "A whole note is 4 beats."}, {"prompt": "Rhythm is...", "options": ["A pattern of long and short sounds", "A colour", "A picture", "A word"], "answer": 0, "why": "Rhythm is a sound pattern."}]}],
        ["Telling a story", "text", 540, "## Art and music tell stories\n{{flow Idea > Characters > Problem > Solution}}\n\nYou can tell a story with:\n- A **drawing** (a comic strip)\n- A **song** (a ballad)\n- A **dance** (movement)\n- A **drum pattern** (rhythm)\n\n> Example: Draw a comic strip with 4 boxes: (1) a boy loses his hat, (2) he looks everywhere, (3) he finds it on a goat, (4) he laughs.\n\n> Tip: Use bold colours for big feelings and soft colours for quiet moments.\n\n> Try it: Plan a 4-box comic about a funny day at school. || Answers vary. Check for a beginning, middle and end.", {"title": "Check your understanding", "questions": [{"prompt": "A story can be told with...", "options": ["Only words", "Drawing, song, dance or drums", "Only numbers", "Only photos"], "answer": 1, "why": "Many art forms tell stories."}, {"prompt": "Which colours show quiet moments?", "options": ["Soft colours", "Only black", "Neon only", "Red only"], "answer": 0, "why": "Soft colours feel quiet."}, {"prompt": "A comic strip is a...", "options": ["Series of drawings that tells a story", "Poem", "Dance", "Number line"], "answer": 0, "why": "Comics tell stories in boxes."}]}],
        ["Sharing your work", "text", 540, "## Show it with pride\nArtists share their work to learn from others.\n\n{{flow Finish > Title it > Explain it > Listen to feedback}}\n\n## Good feedback uses 3 steps\n1. **Say something kind:** \"I love your colours.\"\n2. **Ask a question:** \"How did you make the sky?\"\n3. **Suggest one idea:** \"You could add shadows.\"\n\n> Tip: When someone shares, look closely before you speak.\n\n> Try it: Give kind feedback to a classmate's painting. || For example: \"I like your bright colours. How did you get the sunset? Next time, maybe add some clouds.\"", null],
        ["Creativity quiz", "quiz", 0, "## Final quiz\nAnswer every question, then mark the lesson complete.", {"title": "Creativity quiz", "questions": [{"prompt": "Primary colours are...", "options": ["Red, yellow, blue", "Green, orange, purple", "Black, white, grey", "Pink, brown, green"], "answer": 0, "why": "The three primaries."}, {"prompt": "The foreground of a picture is...", "options": ["The part closest to you", "The sky", "The horizon", "The edge"], "answer": 0, "why": "Nearest part."}, {"prompt": "The beat is...", "options": ["The steady pulse", "The loudest sound", "A song title", "A drum"], "answer": 0, "why": "Steady pulse."}, {"prompt": "Good feedback begins with...", "options": ["Something kind", "A complaint", "Silence", "A joke"], "answer": 0, "why": "Start kindly."}]}],
      ]),
